# OneMind Exports — defensive ignore list.
#
# This repo is PUBLIC-FACING and shares no history with any private vault or
# Keep repo. Everything below is a class of file that has already leaked into
# a staging area at least once (2026-08-13 Construction Yard cleanup found
# 3,062 node_modules files, a real access.json beside its example, and a live
# sent-message state file with a real message ID).
#
# ⚠️ This list is a backstop, NOT the sanitization gate. A file being ignored
#    here does not mean the release passed review. The gate is the release
#    validator; this only prevents the dumbest version of the accident.

# ── build + dependency junk ───────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# ── runtime state: the thing that carries real IDs and real history ───────
state/
runtime/
*.local.json
*.local.yaml
*.local.yml
*.sent-*
*.log

# ── secrets and live config ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Examples and templates are TRACKED on purpose — they are the documentation.
# The live versions never are.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!env.example
*.token
*.key
*.pem
access.json
# tool.json was WRONGLY listed here (2026-08-13, builder error): in OneMind's
# packaging standard, config/tool.json is the REQUIRED PUBLIC MANIFEST, not
# live config. The blanket ignore silently dropped it from BOTH shipped
# packages while filesystem diffs and sampled URL checks passed — git's
# tracked tree is its own verification surface and must be checked as such.
!*.example.json
!*.template.json
!*.example
!*.template

# ── editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ── backups: where stale copies hide and drift ───────────────────────────
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig

# ── personal conversation archives: working area, never a commit ─────────
# Added 2026-09-11 (Cael) during the Migration Loggers hardening pass.
#
# `Lumberjack_Logger/` is the LIVE working area for the migration extractors.
# It currently holds Shannon's complete ChatGPT export (414 conversations,
# ~117 MB of rendered personal history, including intimate ones) and a 22 MB
# Claude App export zip. It was untracked but NOT ignored, so a single
# `git add -A` in this public-facing repo would have staged all of it.
#
# Nothing is lost by ignoring it: these packages ship the way every other
# OneMind package ships -- a deliberate, sanitized export, not by sitting in
# someone's working directory. Per the header above, this is the backstop and
# not the gate.
# The whole tree stays out of THIS repo, code included.
#
# I first refined this to "ignore the data, track the code" -- then ran the
# sanitization scan on what that made trackable, which is the step that decides it:
#   - adapter_claude_code.py hardcodes real absolute paths (C:\Users\<user>\...)
#     and agent home directories
#   - redact_config.py is a personal-info REDACTION RULESET, which is by
#     construction a list of the personal terms, including a real-name pattern
# By the packaging standard these are LIVE/PRIVATE packages, not export-ready ones.
# Private paths are exactly what a OneMind export replaces with placeholders, so
# the code is no more publishable here than the archives are.
#
# Nothing is lost: these ship the way every other OneMind package ships -- a
# deliberate sanitized export. Versioning the working code belongs in a private
# repo, not this one. Backstop, not gate.
Lumberjack_Logger/
